{"term":"condition","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:51611f88bd16de13de","definition":"A state or quality.","example":"National reports on the condition of public education are dismal.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["way"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/condition#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0d9d41a295dc00486d","definition":"A requirement or prerequisite.","example":"Environmental protection is a condition for sustainability.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["requisite","necessity"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/condition#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:193a1222dedcfa9bb4","definition":"A logical clause or phrase that a conditional statement uses. The phrase can either be true or false.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/condition#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4597ac7b021a1d8ee0","definition":"A clause in a contract or agreement indicating that a certain contingency may modify the principal obligation in some way.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/condition#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:181f4600e2b77cacbd","definition":"To subject to the process of acclimation.","example":"I became conditioned to the absence of seasons in San Diego.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["air-condition","conditionability","conditionable","conditioner","miscondition","overcondition","precondition","recondition","uncondition"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/condition#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:75bf9a227b0106126e","definition":"To subject to different conditions, especially as an exercise.","example":"They were conditioning their shins in their karate class.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["air-condition","conditionability","conditionable","conditioner","miscondition","overcondition","precondition","recondition","uncondition"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/condition#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c4b8d22335554f6ced","definition":"To make dependent on a condition to be fulfilled; to make conditional on.","example":"After some opposition, Marianne yielded to her sister's entreaties, and consented to go out […] She expressly conditioned, however, for paying no visits […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["air-condition","conditionability","conditionable","conditioner","miscondition","overcondition","precondition","recondition","uncondition"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/condition#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ed87bc8ae65423ebb3","definition":"To place conditions or limitations upon.","example":"Yet seas that daily gain upon the shore / Have ebb and flow conditioning their march, / And slow and sure comes up the golden year.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["air-condition","conditionability","conditionable","conditioner","miscondition","overcondition","precondition","recondition","uncondition"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/condition#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:cb14007226d6c6c860","definition":"To shape the behaviour of someone to do something.","example":"The children were conditioned to speak up if they had any disagreements.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["air-condition","conditionability","conditionable","conditioner","miscondition","overcondition","precondition","recondition","uncondition"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/condition#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:75cc0288a2062ba35d","definition":"To treat, especially hair with hair conditioner.","example":"Experiments on steep inclines in the United States showed that washing the rails with a detergent to remove oil and grease resulted in a marked improvement; but conditioning the rails with a special neutralising chemical completely eliminated slipping on a bank on which it was so common as to necessitate restriction of trainloads.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["air-condition","conditionability","conditionable","conditioner","miscondition","overcondition","precondition","recondition","uncondition"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/condition#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:da1bd667eb7e45826d","definition":"To contract; to stipulate; to agree.","example":"[P]ay me back my credit, / And I'll condition wi'ye.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["air-condition","conditionability","conditionable","conditioner","miscondition","overcondition","precondition","recondition","uncondition"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/condition#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f1e9eb6b8d9feabc71","definition":"To test or assay, as silk (to ascertain the proportion of moisture it contains).","example":"divers parcel of silk conditioned or assayed","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["air-condition","conditionability","conditionable","conditioner","miscondition","overcondition","precondition","recondition","uncondition"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/condition#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:121524bbf0c1da4124","definition":"To put under conditions; to require to pass a new examination or to make up a specified study, as a condition of remaining in one's class or in college.","example":"to condition a student who has failed in some branch of study","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"US","register":"US, transitive","wordFamily":["air-condition","conditionability","conditionable","conditioner","miscondition","overcondition","precondition","recondition","uncondition"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/condition#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:200043ed7b6e7d7ffd","definition":"To impose upon an object those relations or conditions without which knowledge and thought are alleged to be impossible.","example":"\"To think is thus to condition,\" because it is to know this or that object, and this or that object in a particular mode or condition.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["air-condition","conditionability","conditionable","conditioner","miscondition","overcondition","precondition","recondition","uncondition"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/condition#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/kənˈdɪʃ(ə)n/","us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/9a/En-us-condition.ogg/En-us-condition.ogg.mp3"},"wordFamily":["air-condition","conditionability","conditionable","conditioner","miscondition","overcondition","precondition","recondition","uncondition"]}